# Copy this file to .env. The repo-root .env is ignored by Git and loaded by
# scripts/infra-env.sh when running `make infra-apply ENV=staging|production`.
# Keep provider credentials here only; merchandise_config belongs in the
# environment's ignored OpenTofu tfvars file and must contain no secrets.

# All bootstrapped secrets are environment-scoped. Put the staging value on the
# _STAGING line and the production value on the _PRODUCTION line. The apply
# selects only the suffix matching ENV and never falls back to unscoped values.
# Preserve the current production VIN pepper when filling VIN_PEPPER_PRODUCTION;
# changing it changes HMACs used by existing vehicle data.
#
# Application secrets
# VIN_PEPPER_STAGING=
# RESEND_API_KEY_STAGING=
# IDEAL_POSTCODES_API_KEY_STAGING=
# INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN_STAGING=
#
# VIN_PEPPER_PRODUCTION=
# RESEND_API_KEY_PRODUCTION=
# IDEAL_POSTCODES_API_KEY_PRODUCTION=
# INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN_PRODUCTION=

# Commerce credentials (Stripe test key in staging, live key in production).
# PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN_STAGING=
# PRINTIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET_STAGING=
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY_STAGING=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET_STAGING=whsec_...
#
# PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN_PRODUCTION=
# PRINTIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET_PRODUCTION=
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY_PRODUCTION=sk_live_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET_PRODUCTION=whsec_...
